{
  "video": {
    "id": "CdAgzk5tQhs",
    "title": "Basic Mechanisms of Cloning, excerpt 1 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CdAgzk5tQhs",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 800,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 221,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.34,
      "end": 11.29,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: So, first step, we need to cut our DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 16.34,
      "end": 26.446,
      "duration": 10.106,
      "text": "Step one, cut, which is going to be DNA restriction enzymes."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 35.98,
      "end": 39.91,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "It turns out, quite remarkably, that if I have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 39.91,
      "end": 54.64,
      "duration": 14.73,
      "text": "sequence of DNA, five prime A G C T A G A A T T C T T A C C"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 54.64,
      "end": 58.0,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "three prime, and we'll come backwards"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 58.0,
      "end": 59.25,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "filling in the sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 69.17,
      "end": 77.17,
      "duration": 8.0,
      "text": "It turns out that molecular biologists are so cool that"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 77.17,
      "end": 84.1,
      "duration": 6.93,
      "text": "they invented a protein that is able to recognize that six"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 84.1,
      "end": 88.9,
      "duration": 4.8,
      "text": "letter sequence, G-A-A-T-T-C."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 88.9,
      "end": 93.36,
      "duration": 4.46,
      "text": "And it is able-- actually it's G-A-A-T-T-C on this strand,"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 93.36,
      "end": 95.19,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "but what is it coming back?"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 95.19,
      "end": 99.17,
      "duration": 3.98,
      "text": "It's G-A-A-T-T-C. It's the same thing."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 99.17,
      "end": 101.3,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "So actually this is a palindrome."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 101.3,
      "end": 101.97,
      "duration": 0.67,
      "text": "That's kind of nice."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 101.97,
      "end": 102.99,
      "duration": 1.02,
      "text": "It's a palindrome--"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 102.99,
      "end": 105.22,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "it's a reverse palindrome."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 105.22,
      "end": 110.53,
      "duration": 5.31,
      "text": "It's the same word spelled backwards on the other strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 110.53,
      "end": 116.53,
      "duration": 6.0,
      "text": "So what it does is it cuts it like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 116.53,
      "end": 124.34,
      "duration": 7.81,
      "text": "And what it produces is a DNA molecule like this and a DNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 124.34,
      "end": 128.889,
      "duration": 4.549,
      "text": "molecule like that, that's mostly double stranded, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 128.889,
      "end": 131.5,
      "duration": 2.611,
      "text": "has a four base pair overhang."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 131.5,
      "end": 134.64,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "The overhang reads T-T-A-A here."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 134.64,
      "end": 137.61,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "It reads A-A-T-T there."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 137.61,
      "end": 141.76,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "And remember this is five prime to three prime, five"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 141.76,
      "end": 144.72,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 144.72,
      "end": 146.91,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "And there you go."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 146.91,
      "end": 151.03,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "This guy has its little phosphate at the end there."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 151.03,
      "end": 155.156,
      "duration": 4.126,
      "text": "This guy has his little hydroxyl over there."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 155.156,
      "end": 156.406,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "And it cuts it."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 158.77,
      "end": 161.34,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Now that is an incredible piece of engineering."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 161.34,
      "end": 165.26,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "To come up with a protein, to devise a protein, that is able"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 165.26,
      "end": 168.85,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "to recognize those six bases and cut at those six bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 172.16,
      "end": 173.97,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "And cut in just this way making a really"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 173.97,
      "end": 177.35,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "clean overhang here."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 177.35,
      "end": 180.85,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "It's this cool five prime overhang."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 180.85,
      "end": 184.08,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "Who do you think invented this cool protein?"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 184.08,
      "end": 186.6,
      "duration": 2.52,
      "text": "What engineer came up with this cool protein?"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 186.6,
      "end": 188.32,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: MIT engineers."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 188.32,
      "end": 191.6,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: MIT engineers, yeah."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 191.6,
      "end": 194.27,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "Not a chance."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 195.96,
      "end": 199.01,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "This is a really tough feat."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 199.01,
      "end": 201.61,
      "duration": 2.6,
      "text": "This is something that can only be done by the smartest"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 201.61,
      "end": 202.94,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "engineers on the planet."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 202.94,
      "end": 205.55,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "And MIT engineers are unfortunately only the"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 205.55,
      "end": 207.925,
      "duration": 2.375,
      "text": "smartest human engineers on the planet."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 212.91,
      "end": 215.196,
      "duration": 2.286,
      "text": "Who came up with this is E. coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 215.196,
      "end": 216.94,
      "duration": 1.744,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: So you found it somewhere in nature?"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 216.94,
      "end": 217.49,
      "duration": 0.55,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Sorry?"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 217.49,
      "end": 219.02,
      "duration": 1.53,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: You found it somewhere in nature?"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 219.02,
      "end": 220.95,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Of course you find it somewhere in nature."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 220.95,
      "end": 223.86,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "Almost everything important that we say molecular"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 223.86,
      "end": 227.64,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "biologists have come up with, it means molecular sat at the"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 227.64,
      "end": 232.12,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "feet of the true masters, bacteria, and learned from the"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 232.12,
      "end": 234.31,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "true masters."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 234.31,
      "end": 237.08,
      "duration": 2.77,
      "text": "This protein is found in nature."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 237.08,
      "end": 238.33,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "And it's found in E. coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 241.81,
      "end": 247.09,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "In fact, it's found in E. coli strain R. And it was the first"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 247.09,
      "end": 250.6,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "such protein found in E. coli strain R, so it"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 250.6,
      "end": 252.29,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "gets the name EcoR1."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 256.269,
      "end": 259.269,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "And it cuts the DNA like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 259.269,
      "end": 261.14,
      "duration": 1.871,
      "text": "Pretty cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 263.06,
      "end": 273.82,
      "duration": 10.76,
      "text": "Now, it turns out that E. coli has this EcoR1."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 273.82,
      "end": 275.86,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "How often does E. coli--"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 275.86,
      "end": 278.875,
      "duration": 3.015,
      "text": "so whenever I take EcoR1, this protein, purified from E."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 278.875,
      "end": 283.52,
      "duration": 4.645,
      "text": "coli, and I add it to DNA it always cuts at this site,"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 283.52,
      "end": 286.97,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "which we call an EcoR1 site."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 286.97,
      "end": 288.76,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "How frequently do we expect, what's the"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 288.76,
      "end": 291.12,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "frequency of EcoR1 sites?"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 294.47,
      "end": 299.43,
      "duration": 4.96,
      "text": "G-A-A-T-T-C, how often will that occur at random?"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 302.51,
      "end": 303.243,
      "duration": 0.733,
      "text": "One in--"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 303.243,
      "end": 304.03,
      "duration": 0.787,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Two to the sixth?"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 304.03,
      "end": 305.52,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: One in two to the sixth?"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 305.52,
      "end": 307.28,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "How many letters do I have?"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 307.28,
      "end": 308.79,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Four, oh, four to the sixth."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 308.79,
      "end": 310.09,
      "duration": 1.3,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: One in four to the sixth."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 310.09,
      "end": 313.85,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "My frequency should be about one in four to the sixth,"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 313.85,
      "end": 315.38,
      "duration": 1.53,
      "text": "which is about what?"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 315.38,
      "end": 317.18,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "text": "What's four to the sixth?"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 317.18,
      "end": 318.1,
      "duration": 0.92,
      "text": "It's two to the 12th."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 318.1,
      "end": 319.981,
      "duration": 1.881,
      "text": "It's about 4,000."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 319.981,
      "end": 321.83,
      "duration": 1.849,
      "text": "It's about one in 4,000 letters."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 321.83,
      "end": 325.028,
      "duration": 3.198,
      "text": "One in 4,000 bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 325.028,
      "end": 326.07,
      "duration": 1.042,
      "text": "So it's very convenient."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 326.07,
      "end": 328.78,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "One in every 4,000 bases it'll roughly cut."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 328.78,
      "end": 335.0,
      "duration": 6.22,
      "text": "It'll cut at roughly one 4,000 bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 335.0,
      "end": 337.29,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "Why doesn't E. coli cut its own DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 343.37,
      "end": 345.02,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "If it's got this protein floating around in its cell,"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 345.02,
      "end": 348.61,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "why isn't it chopping up its own DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 348.61,
      "end": 351.37,
      "duration": 2.76,
      "text": "Doesn't have G-A-A-T-T-C?"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 351.37,
      "end": 353.48,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "Yeah, the problem is it's so frequent."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 353.48,
      "end": 354.86,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "That'd be really hard to make sure--"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 354.86,
      "end": 357.68,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "I mean, E. coli has 4 million letters in its genome."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 357.68,
      "end": 359.5,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "This should cut every 4,000 bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 359.5,
      "end": 362.43,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "You expect about 1,000 such sequences."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 362.43,
      "end": 365.45,
      "duration": 3.02,
      "text": "It might be hard to arrange not to cut--"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 365.45,
      "end": 367.6,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "not to have any such sequences."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 367.6,
      "end": 371.125,
      "duration": 3.525,
      "text": "It's a good idea, is not to have any, but an alternative--"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 371.125,
      "end": 372.61,
      "duration": 1.485,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 372.61,
      "end": 373.94,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: It protects them."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 373.94,
      "end": 377.83,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "It turns out E. coli, instead of avoiding the sequence"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 377.83,
      "end": 380.69,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "altogether, has another trick up its sleeve."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 380.69,
      "end": 385.33,
      "duration": 4.64,
      "text": "E. coli protects this sequence whenever it occurs."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 385.33,
      "end": 389.215,
      "duration": 3.885,
      "text": "So it turns out that whenever you have a stretch of the E."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 389.215,
      "end": 398.325,
      "duration": 9.11,
      "text": "coli genome that has this G-A-A-T-T-C in it, what E."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 398.325,
      "end": 401.02,
      "duration": 2.695,
      "text": "coli does is it puts--"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 401.02,
      "end": 403.8,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "I'm just writing M-E here for a methyl group."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 403.8,
      "end": 405.4,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "Right, C-H three up there."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 405.4,
      "end": 406.59,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "It puts a methyl group--"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 406.59,
      "end": 408.01,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "I'll write C-H three."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 408.01,
      "end": 409.51,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "There we go."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 409.51,
      "end": 414.62,
      "duration": 5.11,
      "text": "It puts a methyl group on the A, that middle A."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 414.62,
      "end": 419.9,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "Well, that is a cute trick that E. coli uses, putting a"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 419.9,
      "end": 421.15,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "methyl group there."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 423.62,
      "end": 426.63,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "Because what happens is, when there's a methyl group, right"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 426.63,
      "end": 431.93,
      "duration": 5.3,
      "text": "at that position, the enzyme no longer recognizes and no"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 431.93,
      "end": 433.18,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "longer cuts there."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 435.97,
      "end": 438.77,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "So that's kind of clever."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 438.77,
      "end": 441.555,
      "duration": 2.785,
      "text": "E. coli makes this protein that can recognize"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 441.555,
      "end": 445.66,
      "duration": 4.105,
      "text": "G-A-A-T-T-C, but it has a second protein that puts"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 445.66,
      "end": 447.2,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "methyl groups there."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 447.2,
      "end": 450.83,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "And this protein happens by accident"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 450.83,
      "end": 452.54,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "to be called a methylase."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 456.72,
      "end": 458.03,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "It has a methylase."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 458.03,
      "end": 460.93,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "And the methylase protects that sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 460.93,
      "end": 464.18,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "So now, this is really cool engineering, but kind of dumb."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 464.18,
      "end": 465.23,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "What's it doing there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 465.23,
      "end": 467.23,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "It has something that cuts the sequence and it protects the"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 467.23,
      "end": 470.55,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "sequence, why bother having this?"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 470.55,
      "end": 472.392,
      "duration": 1.842,
      "text": "Yeah?"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 472.392,
      "end": 477.232,
      "duration": 4.84,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: You can use it to cut it at places to unwrap the"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 477.232,
      "end": 478.2,
      "duration": 0.968,
      "text": "true strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 478.2,
      "end": 479.41,
      "duration": 1.21,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: That's an interesting idea."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 479.41,
      "end": 482.14,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "We could use it to cut our DNA and open it up to unravel our"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 482.14,
      "end": 483.01,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "true strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 483.01,
      "end": 483.82,
      "duration": 0.81,
      "text": "It's a thought."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 483.82,
      "end": 484.71,
      "duration": 0.89,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 484.71,
      "end": 488.15,
      "duration": 3.44,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: To protect the bacteria from viruses?"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 488.15,
      "end": 491.03,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Protect the bacteria from viruses."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 491.03,
      "end": 492.485,
      "duration": 1.455,
      "text": "How do you protect yourself from viruses?"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 495.45,
      "end": 497.54,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "Well, you have an immune system with immune cells and"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 497.54,
      "end": 498.57,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "antibodies and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 498.57,
      "end": 500.93,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "Does E. coli have an immune system?"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 500.93,
      "end": 502.215,
      "duration": 1.285,
      "text": "Why doesn't it have immune cells?"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 504.84,
      "end": 506.01,
      "duration": 1.17,
      "text": "Because it's like one cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 506.01,
      "end": 508.71,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "How's it going to have an immune system, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 508.71,
      "end": 510.32,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "So suppose E. coli gets a cold."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 510.32,
      "end": 512.7,
      "duration": 2.38,
      "text": "Suppose it gets infected by a virus."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 512.7,
      "end": 515.61,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "How's it going to protect itself?"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 515.61,
      "end": 519.83,
      "duration": 4.22,
      "text": "Cut at a frequently occurring DNA sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 519.83,
      "end": 525.72,
      "duration": 5.89,
      "text": "Now the virus, of course, isn't methylated there, bingo."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 525.72,
      "end": 527.1,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "That's how it tells its own--"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 527.1,
      "end": 529.08,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "you can tell cell from an invader."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 532.71,
      "end": 535.52,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "E. coli can tell cell from an invader because it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 535.52,
      "end": 539.59,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "methylated its own G-A-A-T-T-C sites, but the virus isn't"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 539.59,
      "end": 541.13,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "methylated there."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 541.13,
      "end": 542.98,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "Way cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 542.98,
      "end": 544.88,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "This is an immune system for E. coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 548.62,
      "end": 550.44,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "Now, it turns out-- so this is protection."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 550.44,
      "end": 561.46,
      "duration": 11.02,
      "text": "These restriction enzymes protect E. coli from viruses."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 570.17,
      "end": 572.75,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "It turns out that E. coli is not alone"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 572.75,
      "end": 574.58,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "in this clever trick."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 574.58,
      "end": 578.77,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "It turns out that other bacteria have also thought of"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 578.77,
      "end": 580.27,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "this trick."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 580.27,
      "end": 583.87,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "So it turns out that there is another restriction enzyme"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 583.87,
      "end": 594.04,
      "duration": 10.17,
      "text": "that cuts at G-G-A-T-C-C. And on the other strand it goes"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 594.04,
      "end": 601.75,
      "duration": 7.71,
      "text": "G-G-A-T-C-C. It, again, cuts in that distinctive pattern."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 601.75,
      "end": 604.005,
      "duration": 2.255,
      "text": "And it's called BamH1."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 608.971,
      "end": 610.65,
      "duration": 1.679,
      "text": "And there's another guy."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 610.65,
      "end": 620.06,
      "duration": 9.41,
      "text": "And he cuts at A-A-G-C-T-T, A-A-G-C-T-T. And it"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 620.06,
      "end": 622.04,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "also cuts like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 622.04,
      "end": 624.82,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "And it's called HindIII."
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 628.004,
      "end": 632.96,
      "duration": 4.956,
      "text": "And there's some that cut at G-A-T-C, just"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 632.96,
      "end": 634.39,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "the four letter word."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 636.95,
      "end": 639.17,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "And they cut like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 639.17,
      "end": 654.79,
      "duration": 15.62,
      "text": "And there's some that cut at C-A-G-C-T-G, C-A-G-C-T-G, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 654.79,
      "end": 658.38,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "this, cuts smack in the middle."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 658.38,
      "end": 662.69,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "In other words, there's a wide number of different tricks."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 662.69,
      "end": 664.37,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "Some cut at six bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 664.37,
      "end": 665.74,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "Some cut at four bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 665.74,
      "end": 667.59,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "Some cut at eight bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 667.59,
      "end": 669.71,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "Some cut leaving an overhang."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 669.71,
      "end": 671.64,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "Some cut smack in the middle."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 671.64,
      "end": 675.67,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "Some cut leaving the overhang in the other direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 675.67,
      "end": 678.24,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Some allow a degenerate base in the middle."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 678.24,
      "end": 681.35,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "It doesn't care which base is in the middle."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 681.35,
      "end": 684.11,
      "duration": 2.76,
      "text": "There's a zillion different solutions that bacteria have"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 684.11,
      "end": 686.39,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "come up with for their immune system."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 686.39,
      "end": 690.39,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "And so, if I want to cut up some human DNA all I need is"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 690.39,
      "end": 695.42,
      "duration": 5.03,
      "text": "say, this protein EcoR1 or BamH1 or HindIII or MVL 1 or"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 695.42,
      "end": 697.695,
      "duration": 2.275,
      "text": "PVU 2 or et cetera."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 697.695,
      "end": 700.71,
      "duration": 3.015,
      "text": "And I can do that by growing up E. coli and"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 700.71,
      "end": 701.96,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "purifying the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 704.81,
      "end": 708.01,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "And if I wanted HindIII, I would grow up haemophilus"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 708.01,
      "end": 711.06,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "influenza and purify the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 711.06,
      "end": 713.89,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "So in a molecular biology lab, today, if you want to cut up"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 713.89,
      "end": 718.0,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "human DNA, you could grow up some E. coli and purify EcoR1"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 718.0,
      "end": 719.25,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "or haemophilus influenza."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 721.26,
      "end": 724.71,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "And that is indeed what ancient molecular biologists"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 724.71,
      "end": 729.36,
      "duration": 4.65,
      "text": "did in prehistoric days in the 1970s and 1980s."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 729.36,
      "end": 733.0,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "They would purify their own restriction enzymes."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 733.0,
      "end": 734.09,
      "duration": 1.09,
      "text": "They're still alive today."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 734.09,
      "end": 735.4,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "You can talk to them."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 735.4,
      "end": 737.14,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "There are many of them on the faculty."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 737.14,
      "end": 740.01,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "And they'll tell you how it put hair on their chest to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 740.01,
      "end": 742.265,
      "duration": 2.255,
      "text": "able to purify their own restriction enzymes."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 747.61,
      "end": 750.15,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "What do you do today?"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 750.15,
      "end": 753.275,
      "duration": 3.125,
      "text": "Order it online from the catalog, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 753.275,
      "end": 756.065,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "You know, there's the catalog, the New"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 756.065,
      "end": 758.48,
      "duration": 2.415,
      "text": "England Bio Labs catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 758.48,
      "end": 759.73,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Let's see what we got here."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 763.8,
      "end": 773.47,
      "duration": 9.67,
      "text": "Restriction enzymes, modifying enzymes, polymerases, all"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 773.47,
      "end": 779.15,
      "duration": 5.68,
      "text": "right, EcoR1, sale on EcoR1 right now."
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 779.15,
      "end": 784.07,
      "duration": 4.92,
      "text": "$100 buys you 10,000 units of EcoR1."
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 784.07,
      "end": 785.03,
      "duration": 0.96,
      "text": "It's in the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 785.03,
      "end": 785.78,
      "duration": 0.75,
      "text": "You can go online."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 785.78,
      "end": 786.27,
      "duration": 0.49,
      "text": "You can order it."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 786.27,
      "end": 788.39,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "You can have it tomorrow by FedEx."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 788.39,
      "end": 790.48,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "So, but that's how it works."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 790.48,
      "end": 791.81,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "It's in the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 791.81,
      "end": 795.93,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "So you can get any restriction enzyme you want to cut DNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 795.93,
      "end": 797.18,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "anywhere you want to."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Biology & Chemistry",
    "title": "Introduction to Biology",
    "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLF83B8D8C87426E44"
  }
}